From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bezilaszlo <bezilaszlo95@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:13:08 +0200
Subject: fix(backlight): correct LM3697 brightness writes

Control B brightness uses LSB register 0x22[2:0] and MSB register
0x23[7:0]. The LM3697 latches the value when the MSB is written, so
write the low three bits first and the upper eight bits second. The
previous driver sent the bytes to the opposite registers and did not
mask the LSB, producing incorrect hardware brightness values.

The KTD3136 path and LM3697 readback decoding are unchanged.

Fixes: 034e25ff19f4 ("backlight: add Kinetic KTD3136 and TI LM3697 driver")
Link: https://www.ti.com/lit/gpn/lm3697
Signed-off-by: bezilaszlo <bezilaszlo95@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/video/backlight/ktd3136.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/ktd3136.c b/drivers/video/backlight/ktd3136.c
index d8925d0cd..7494a420f 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/ktd3136.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/ktd3136.c
@@ -32,8 +32,8 @@
 #define KTD3136_CTRL_LINEAR	BIT(1)
 #define KTD3136_PWM_DISABLE	0x9b	/* PWM off, CH1+CH2 like 0x1b */
 
-#define LM3697_REG_BRT_MSB	0x22
-#define LM3697_REG_BRT_LSB	0x23
+#define LM3697_REG_BRT_MSB	0x23
+#define LM3697_REG_BRT_LSB	0x22
 #define LM3697_REG_READBACK_BRT_LSB	0x22
 #define LM3697_REG_READBACK_BRT_MSB	0x23
 #define LM3697_REG_BANK_ENABLE	0x24
@@ -104,12 +104,12 @@ static int ktd3136_set_lm3697(struct ktd3136 *ktd, unsigned int brightness)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* Preserve the existing 0x23-then-0x22 sequence for this diagnostic. */
-	ret = ktd3136_write(ktd, LM3697_REG_BRT_LSB, brightness & 0xff);
+	/* The LM3697 latches brightness when the MSB is written. */
+	ret = ktd3136_write(ktd, LM3697_REG_BRT_LSB, brightness & 0x7);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = ktd3136_write(ktd, LM3697_REG_BRT_MSB, (brightness >> 8) & 0x7);
+	ret = ktd3136_write(ktd, LM3697_REG_BRT_MSB, (brightness >> 3) & 0xff);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
